Z7kW5jmPKZ7RTvBCW7XD3T99hq2R_d54cK004" style=3D"color:#192733" data-hs-link=
-id=3D"0" data-hs-link-id-v2=3D"nE24HOm0" target=3D"_blank">per</a> <span s=
tyle=3D"font-style: italic;">Business Insider</span>.&nbsp;<br><br></p>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%; font-weight:bold; font-size:18px">Why?&nbsp;<=
br><br></p>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%">Trains not only rule for the aforementioned r=
easons, but they=E2=80=99ve also been getting better.&nbsp;<br><br></p>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%">Amtrak, which is largely owned by the US gove=
rnment, has made a number of improvements in recent years to both its train=
s and stations, helping to curb delays =E2=80=94 especially on its shorter =
routes, which are the ones passengers use most often.&nbsp;<br><br></p>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%">At the same time, other forms of transit kind=
a suck. <br><br>Amtrak travelers can read a book, catch up on work, or do a=
 crossword puzzle, whereas drivers are stuck paying constant attention and =
gritting their teeth through gridlock.&nbsp;<br><br></p>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%">Then there=E2=80=99s flying. Driven in part b=
y&nbsp;factors like labor shortages and the rising cost of jet fuel, airlin=
e fares were up <a href=3D"https://media.hubspot.com/e3t/Ctc/UB+113/d2q-Vf0=
4/VWbCL48sBSndW3bMVkZ8-qV5wW4nNzqf5Jk5X1N50kgP22-ZW0W7lCdLW6lZ3mDW70JsNs212=
jv3W3W1JbF1j9xrXW7yp70S4RS7tNW2L7P4L5ZV43HW7WdwP02LYZQyW5VGB684Vt9vyW3l53Xv=
